* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-closed-loop-lock (issue #150, Part of #16)
* RECORD-006 OPEN-LOOP charge-per-pulse bench for the mitigated `cp`
* (cp_cascbias snapshot or a RECORD-006 variant of it, see cpdiag_build.py).
*
* The cp is driven directly by ideal pulse sources on UP and DN (no pfd, no
* loop), VOUT is held at a fixed @VOUT@ V by an ideal source, and the
* current delivered into that source is measured through the 0 V probe
* `Vpr` (i(Vpr) > 0 = current into the filter side, i.e. UP-type charge).
* Isolated UP-only, DN-only and simultaneous (UP=DN, "both") pulses of three
* widths are applied, @SPACING@ apart, so the charge-per-pulse
*     Q(w) = I_plateau * w + Q0
* separates the DC plateau term (slope, includes any up/dn mismatch) from the
* per-pulse switching/injection term (intercept Q0).  Bias, supply, IREF,
* corner, temperature identical to the closed-loop diagnostic deck.
* DIAGNOSTIC DECK -- NOT THE COMMITTED PLL.  The pulse list (@EVENTS@ in the
* generated deck's comments) is written by run_cp_pulse_charge.sh.

.lib $PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib $PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!

.include pll_blocks_cpdiag.spice
.include cpdiag_models.inc

Vsub sub! 0 dc 0
Vdd_cp vdd_cp 0 dc @VDD@

Irefbp ibp 0 dc @IREF@
Irefcp icp 0 dc @IREF@
Irefbn 0 ibn dc @IREF@
Irefcn 0 icn dc @IREF@

* pulse drive: PWL files generated by the runner
Vup up 0 pwl(@UPPWL@)
Vdn dn 0 pwl(@DNPWL@)

XCP up dn ibp icp ibn icn vcp vdd_cp 0 cp
Vpr vcp vout dc 0
Vout vout 0 dc @VOUT@

.tran @TPRINT@ @TSTOP@ 0 @TMAX@

.control
run
meas tran i_cp_avg_quiet avg i(Vdd_cp) from=20n to=90n
meas tran i_out_quiet avg i(Vpr) from=20n to=90n
meas tran vdump_quiet avg v(xcp.vdump) from=20n to=90n
* switch-common nodes of each leg (drain of the cascode XM2, shared by
* XSWO/XSWD): their off-state level vs VOUT is the step each sees at UP/DN
* turn-on.  "_on" = level near the end of the 6.4 ns simultaneous pulse.
meas tran vswp_quiet avg v(xcp.xlegp.sw) from=20n to=90n
meas tran vswn_quiet avg v(xcp.xlegn.sw) from=20n to=90n
meas tran vswp_on find v(xcp.xlegp.sw) at=586.2n
meas tran vswn_on find v(xcp.xlegn.sw) at=586.2n
print i_cp_avg_quiet i_out_quiet vdump_quiet vswp_quiet vswn_quiet vswp_on vswn_on
wrdata cppulse.dat v(up) v(dn) i(Vpr) v(xcp.vdump)
.endc
.end
